        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0104" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1950-55Intel/pg75"/>

                <head>42. Note From the Executive Secretary of the National Security Council
                        (Lay) to the National Security Council<anchor n="1" xml:id="d42-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">NSC 10/4</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-16">January 16,
                        1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">RESPONSIBILITIES OF CIA
                        (OPC) WITH RESPECT TO GUERRILLA WARFARE</p>
                <p rendition="#center">References: NSC 10/2 and
                        NSC 10/3<anchor n="2" xml:id="d42-f2"/></p>
                <p>Upon the recommendation of the Acting Director of Central Intelligence, his
                    enclosed memorandum and its attached draft Directive on the subject are
                    circulated herewith for consideration by the National Security Council.</p>
                <p>As recommended in paragraph 3 of the enclosed memorandum, the Departments of
                    State and Defense and the Joint Chiefs of Staff are being requested to transmit
                    to this office their respective comments for Council consideration in connection
                    with the enclosed draft Directive.</p>
                <pb facs="0105" n="76" xml:id="pg76"/>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">It is requested that special security precautions be
                        taken in the handling of this matter</hi>.</p>
                <closer><signed>James S. Lay,
                        Jr.</signed><anchor n="3" xml:id="d42-f3"/></closer>




                <xi:include href="d42-a1.xml" xpointer="d42-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d42-a2.xml" xpointer="d42-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Truman Library, Papers of
                        Harry S. Truman, President’s
                    Secretary’s Files, Subject File. Top Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f2" n="2" xml:id="d42-f2-content">
                <p>For text of NSC 10/2, see <ref
                        target="frus1945-50Intel#d292"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1945–1950, Emergence of the Intelligence Establishment,
                        Document 292</ref>. DCI
                    Smith’s interpretation of NSC 10/2 as conveyed by Wisner to the Departments of State and Defense and JCS is printed in <hi rendition="#italic">The
                            CIA Under Harry Truman</hi>, p. 347. A draft of NSC 10/3 is in <ref target="frus1945-50Intel#d419"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1945–1950, Emergence of
                        the Intelligence Establishment, Document 419</ref>. Other versions are
                    attachments to <ref target="#d38">Documents 38</ref> and <ref target="#d43"
                        >43</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f3" n="3" xml:id="d42-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
